[agent:result]       752→# --- `mlpab run` must be FOREGROUND, never piped or backgrounded ---------------
[agent:result]       753→# A nested `mlpab run` (spawned from inside another agent session) must stay
[agent:result]       754→# synchronous. Two fatal ways a caller tries to "background" it:
[agent:result]       755→#   - Piping (`mlpab run … | head`/`| tail`): downstream exits after N lines and
[agent:result]       756→#     SIGPIPE-kills `mlpab run` mid-build, but the Bash tool returns 0 (head's
[agent:result]       757→#     exit), so the caller reads truncated build output, thinks the run
